! Collision brief, wave 2 of the cut reads (2026-10-31)

Operator, verbatim: "collide each spirit's findings with another Sonnet cold reader that has internet research caps, then land all of their 2-wave researches into the meme."

You collide with ONE wave-1 cut-read report. You read cold: you wrote neither the code nor the report. Your job is adversarial. Try to BREAK each finding and each verdict, and keep only what survives.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/read-first`>>

!! Read first
* /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/scouts/cut-reads/COMMON.md: the wave-1 brief. Its laws and fences bind you too.
* Your target report: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/scouts/cut-reads/&lt;batch>.md
* The design meme: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/test-recut-road.mem

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/do`>>

!! Do
# ''Re-verify every FINDING against the code, in full.'' Read the whole function and its callers, not the reporter's excerpt. Trace the actual runtime order, including async/microtask order, event listeners and the order composeCoreVessel calls stages in. For each finding, rule CONFIRMED, REFUTED or NARROWED, and give your evidence (file:line). Say whether it fails open or closed, and its real reach. Sketch the smallest red test that would prove it.
# ''Re-verify every verdict'' (CUT-READY / NEEDS-RULING / DO-NOT-CUT). Look for hidden callers the reporter missed, including tools/, tests, string-keyed lookups, TW5 module titles and `.mem` canon. For each NEEDS-RULING lean, say whether you agree, and why.
# ''Internet research.'' Use WebSearch/WebFetch, or the web-fetch agent if the tools aren't direct. Prefer primary sources and date-stamp them (today is 2026-10-31). Find outside precedent and pitfalls for each finding's class and each cut's pattern, for example:
#* fail-closed defaults and TOCTOU in access gates
#* stale-read/refresh ordering in membership revocation
#* Automerge Repo `sharePolicy` semantics
#* TiddlyWiki module-type startup ordering
#* vitest fixture and characterization-test practice
#* dependency injection without process globals
#* functional core / imperative shell

Mark each source read or search-only. Weigh outside practice against house law (web3-only, no global now, capability not host, red-first, old shapes burn), and say where they conflict.
# ''Find what wave 1 missed'' in its span: new findings, at the TOP.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/fences`>>

!! Fences
READ-ONLY on the repo. No edits except your one output file. No git writes, suites, boots or builds.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/output`>>

!! Output
Write /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/scouts/cut-reads/&lt;batch>-collide.md. If the write is refused, return it as text. Shape:
* New findings
* Per-finding rulings
* Per-verdict rulings
* Sources
* Merged recommendation per candidate: the final verdict, its red-first shape, and its lean

Hand back under 300 words.

Stand the whole house (CLAUDE.md seed: Personas by name, L-Prime). Your tag: `<Name>: Lares (Tasked Spirit)`.

